         <div type="edition">
            <ab xml:lang="Egyd-Egydol egy-deme">
               <pb n="R" />
               <lb n="1" rend="right-to-left" /><persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p1270">Nꜣ-nfr-ı͗b-Rꜥ-m-ꜣḫ.t</persName>
               <damage degree="high">sm</damage> r <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p9915">Ns-<supplied cert="high" evidence="parallel" reason="lost">H̱nm-</supplied>pꜣ-mtr</persName>
               <rs ref="ancient_titles.xml#idt219" type="title">pꜣ <supplied cert="high" reason="lost">mr-</supplied>šn </rs>ı͗ ḏı͗ <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#d45">Pꜣ-Rꜥ</persName>
               <lb n="2" />qy pꜣy=f ꜥḥꜥ ḏı͗=k mtr ḥꜣ.ṱ(=y) n pꜣ ¼ n nꜣ ḥḏ(.w) r.ḏı͗=k r.r=w n <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p1195"><damage degree="high">Inḫy(?)</damage></persName>
               <note>For the rejected reading Pẖe cf. Den Brinker / Muhs / Vleeming, DBL (2005), 49.</note>
               <lb n="3" />r ḏı͗.t st n=y ḏı͗=k st n=y ḥꜣ.ṱ(=y) mtr(.w) n.ı͗m=w ı͗w(=y) r ḏi.t wy <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p1195"><damage degree="high">Inḫy(?)</damage></persName>
               <note>For the rejected reading Pẖe cf. Den Brinker / Muhs / Vleeming, DBL (2005), 49.</note>
               <lb n="4" />r.r=k n.ı͗m=w ı͗w(=y) tm ḏı͗.t wy=f ı͗w(=y) r ḏı͗.t n=k ḥḏ (dbn) 5 ı͗wty <lb n="5" />ḏd qnb nb n pꜣ tꜣ ı͗rm=k n-ḏr.t <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p1270">Nꜣ-nfr-ı͗b-Rꜥ-m-ꜣḫ.t sꜣ <surname><damage>Pꜣ-ẖrṱ</damage></surname></persName>
               <lb n="6" />n <date notAfter="-492-06-01" notBefore="-492-06-01" when-custom="Darius_I:30">ḥsb.t 30 ı͗bd 2 pr.t sw 16</date>
               <lb n="7" /><persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p620">I͗ꜥḥ-ı͗.ı͗r-ḏı͗-s sꜣ <surname>Bn-pw-H̱nm-ḫꜣꜥ-r.r=w</surname></persName>
               <lb n="8" /><persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p760"><damage>Ns-bꜣ-nb-ḏd.t</damage>
                  <note>Reading variant Zauzich, P. Berl. Eleph. 1 (1978): Ns-bꜣ.</note> sꜣ <surname><damage>Ḥr-</damage>wḏꜣ</surname></persName>
               <lb n="9" /><persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p9470">Ns-pꜣ-mtr-šps</persName>
               <rs ref="ancient_titles.xml#idt271" type="title">pꜣ ḥm-nṯr 4.nw</rs><lb n="10" /><persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p1350">Wsı͗r-wr sꜣ <surname><damage degree="high">Pꜣ-r.ḏı͗-Inp</damage></surname></persName>
               <note>Thesaurus Linguae Aegyptiae gives here only „Pete...“.</note>
            </ab>
         </div>
         <div type="translation" xml:lang="en">
            <ab xml:lang=" en">
               <pb n="" />
               <lb n="1" />Nepherpremachis greets Es[chnoum]pmetis, the [le]sonis. Oh may Pre <lb n="2" />cause his lifetime to be long! You have satisfied (my) heart with the ¼ of the money, which you have transcribed to Inchy(?), <lb n="3" />in order to give them to me (by Inchy). You have given them to me (by yourself). (My) heart is satisfied with them. (I) will cause Inchy(?) to withdraw <lb n="4" />from you with respect to it. If (I) do not cause him to withdraw from you, (I) will endow you with 5 silver (deben), without <lb n="5" />taking any lawsuit on earth against you. Issued by Nepherpremachis, son of Parates, <lb n="6" />in the 30th regnal year, 16th of Mecheir.<lb n="7" />Artais, son of Benpouchnoumchaaroys, <lb n="8" />Esbendetis, son of [Har]yothes, <lb n="9" />Espmetsepsis, the fourth priest, <lb n="10" />Osoroeris, son of Petenouphis. </ab>
         </div>
